    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/55264>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "If the former be greater than either of the other two, the outside angle will be less than 120°; and if the tension along the surface _cc′_ be as much or more than the sum of the other two, then the drops will stand in contact only, save for the possible effect of external pressure, at a point.".
